{"type": "tool_call", "n": 17, "ts": 1790154699.796258, "tool": "submit_memo", "args": {"text": "MARCH 2026 BANK RECONCILIATION - DE OPERATING ACCOUNT (GL 1000)\n\nRECONCILIATION COMPLETED\n\nGL Ending Balance (after adjustments): EUR 363,817.86\nBank Statement Closing Balance:       EUR 342,467.86\nReconciling Difference:               EUR 21,350.00\n\nADJUSTMENTS POSTED:\n\n1. JE-00309 (Reversal): Reversed duplicate Rheinbyte Software payment\n   - Entry JE-00273 was an exact duplicate of JE-00272\n   - Bank statement shows only one transaction\n   - Adjustment: +EUR 6,480.00\n\n2. JE-00310 (Expense): Posted bank monthly service charge\n   - Date: 2026-03-31\n   - Amount: EUR 38.50\n   - Support: DOC-0202 (Bank Statement)\n   - Adjustment: -EUR 38.50\n\nRECONCILING ITEMS (NET DIFFERENCE EXPLAINED):\n\n1. Undeposited Receipt - JE-00308 (Kessler AG RE-7090): EUR 18,200.00\n   \u2713 APPROVED - No action required\n   Supporting Document: DOC-0206 (Remittance advice)\n   Reason: Payment initiated on 2026-03-31 after bank cut-off. Correctly recorded in GL and will appear on April bank statement. This is normal treasury management for month-end transactions.\n\n2. Unrecorded Payment - BT-DE-0045 (TX-44817): EUR (3,150.00)\n   \u26a0 FLAGGED FOR CONTROLLER REVIEW - Exception ID: EXC-001\n   Issue: Appears on bank statement dated 2026-03-19 but has no GL entry or supporting documentation\n   Action Required: Controller must identify the underlying transaction (vendor, invoice, purpose) and post to GL with proper documentation.\n   Supporting Document: DOC-0202 (Bank Statement)\n\nRECONCILIATION VERIFICATION:\nGL Balance (363,817.86) - Undeposited Kessler (18,200) - Unrecorded Payment (3,150) = Bank Balance (342,467.86) \u2713\n\nThe account reconciles when all identified items are accounted for. The single outstanding item requiring action is the identification and GL posting of the TX-44817 SEPA payment."}, "is_error": false, "result": {"status": "memo submitted; task complete"}, "ms": 9}
